  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto has been actively fostering diplomatic and economic ties both regionally and internationally. Following his engagement at the APEC summit, where he advocated for openness and innovation, the Indonesian government has moved to solidify agreements in diverse fields. Notable developments include a collaboration with the United States for small modular nuclear reactor research and a pact with the Netherlands regarding waste management, formalized during COP31. Domestically, the government and state-owned enterprises are prioritizing sustainable initiatives, with Pertamina partnering with banks to advance green energy financing. Furthermore, the Ministry of Transportation is expanding cooperation with the International Civil Aviation Organization to promote sustainable aviation practices. These strategic alliances reflect a broader effort to align Indonesia's national interests with global standards in environmental, social, and economic sectors.",
